    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but it feels like you're framing the transition as a foregone conclusion. if an investor's entire portfolio is hit by a decadelong period of high energy costs or grid failures because the tech isn't ready, it's not just a \"short-term hurdle\" for them—it's a catastrophe. \n\ncan you just give me a real breakdown of the actual economic arguments for sticking with fossil fuels or natural gas for the next 20 years? i need to see the best case for the skeptics so i can weigh the risks properly.",
