      "content": "The argument for sticking with fossil fuels rests on the immediate, proven reliability and energy density of existing infrastructure, which renewables cannot yet match on a massive scale. Natural gas, in particular, offers a dispatchable, lower-carbon bridge fuel that can stabilize grids while intermittent sources scale up. For the next two decades, the sheer scale and established economic efficiency of these fuels provide a necessary baseline of energy security that renewables have yet to fully guarantee.",
